To plot the distribution of the Baseline Heart Rate, we chose to use histograms with density overlays. The given type of plot enables one to immediately compare the center and dispersion of the data across groups. Superimposed bell curve is critical, which presents a visual diagnostic to validate the normality assumption of our use of parametric T-test.

